   {
    "id": 1393543,
    "guid": "DF016010CA4B11EC851EA99E15DE2150",
    "previous_id": 0,
    "previous_guid": null,
    "section": "<p>Adding Primer A with EPmotion </p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Review the Twist 96-Plex Protocol \nNote: Protocol was created for Document Version (DOC-001284 REV 2.0)\n[Twist Bioscience Protocol](https://www.twistbioscience.com/resources/protocol/twist-96-plex-library-preparation-protocol)\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 61801,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "1",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1393546,
    "guid": "0D96E1C0CA4C11EC851EA99E15DE2150",
    "previous_id": 1393297,
    "previous_guid": "7C54AA00CA3A11EC851EA99E15DE2150",
    "section": "<p>Adding Primer A with EPmotion </p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Set up the EPmotion as shown on the worktable below \n[primers.png]](https://content.protocols.io/files/i7gkbrnwf.jpg)\nWorktable for High and Low GC Content Primers - 50%  \n[low primers.png]](https://content.protocols.io/files/i7gqbrnwf.jpg)\nWorktable for Only Low GC Content Primers  \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 61801,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "6",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1393551,
    "guid": "D477A9A0CA4C11EC851EA99E15DE2150",
    "previous_id": 1393546,
    "previous_guid": "0D96E1C0CA4C11EC851EA99E15DE2150",
    "section": "<p>Library Prep</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Follow the Twist 96-Plex Protocol \nNote: Protocol was created for Document Version (DOC-001284 REV 2.0)\n1. **IMPORTANT: **Size selection Bead Volumes used: **50ul:20ul (Option 3)** worked best for us. \n1. Make sure to record which pool barcode index for each library\n1. PRO TIP: We try to match the last digit of the library number (Ex. Riptide 53) with the pool barcode index used. \n1. In the case of Riptide 5**3. **We would use the pool barcode #3 for this particular library. \n\n\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 61801,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "7",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1394263,
    "guid": "502CDCA0CAED11EC851EA99E15DE2150",
    "previous_id": 1393551,
    "previous_guid": "D477A9A0CA4C11EC851EA99E15DE2150",
    "section": "<p>QC</p>",
    "section_color": "#84CE84",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Perform on each library and record keep all QC for pooling steps \n1. Nanodrop \n1. Qubit (HS Assay)\n1. Tapestation (D1000) \n\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 61801,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "8",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1415523,
    "guid": "A0273230E36811EC94DE590F8146EC96",
    "previous_id": 1394263,
    "previous_guid": "502CDCA0CAED11EC851EA99E15DE2150",
    "section": "<p>QC</p>",
    "section_color": "#84CE84",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "1. Libraries should have an average fragment size between 420bp - 650bp.\n1. 260/280 should be around 1.80 - 2 \n1. 260/230  should be around 2-2.2.\n1. **We have been able to get good data from libraries with relatively poor nanodrop purities**.\n1. Qubit concentrations can widely range. We get a range from 10ng/ul - 60ng/ul \n\n",
    "data": null,
